usage() {
    cat <<EOF
Usage: $PROG [--user | --system | --dest DIR] [options]

Installs the offline voice engine data for Shadow Assistant (~700 MB download).

Where:
  --user              ~/.local/share/shadow/voice (\$XDG_DATA_HOME) — default when not root
  --system            /var/lib/shadow-voice — default for root
  --dest DIR          any data root (e.g. a chroot's /usr/share/shadow-voice for an ISO)
What:
  --stt MODEL         moonshine | whisper | both (default both: --calibrate can then pick
                      the model that understands you best)
  --numpy MODE        auto (default: the numpy wheel only when Debian's python3-numpy is
                      not importable) | system (never) | wheel (always)
  --python PATH       Python used to unpack wheels and to pick the numpy wheel (default python3)
Downloads:
  --cache DIR         download cache (default ~/.cache/shadow-voice, /var/cache/shadow-voice as root)
  --offline-cache DIR take every artifact from DIR (file names as published); no network
  --keep-cache        keep the downloaded archives after a successful install
Other actions:
  --check             verify the installed files against manifest.json (sha256)
  --uninstall         remove the installed data (and the download cache)
Behaviour:
  --yes               do not ask for confirmation
  --install-deps      apt-get install missing Debian packages (python3-numpy, espeak-ng, a
                      capture/playback tool, curl, bzip2) with sudo, non-interactively
  --no-selftest       skip "shadow-voiced --selftest" after installing
  --progress-json     one JSON line per step on stdout: {"step","progress":0..1,"message"}
  -h, --help          this help;  --version  print the version

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 unexpected error, 2 usage, 3 missing dependency, 4 download failed,
5 checksum/size mismatch, 6 not enough disk space, 7 permission denied, 8 unpack/install
failed, 9 installed but the selftest failed, 10 --check found problems, 11 nothing
installed, 12 another setup is running, 130 interrupted.
EOF
}

while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
